    description: "STATEMENT: a Go receiver whose type the source states is typed. OBSERVED, not typed by the analyzer after batch 5b: a range variable (the element type of the ranged slice or map), the result of an interface method (only method_declarations record a return type), a call returning two named types (ctx, _ := caddy.NewContext(..)), a composite literal used as a call's operand, an anonymous struct field. The 5 lost edges a blind judge found right before (of 15) are all of these (2 range variables over a slice of an interface type, 2 NewContext results, 1 package variable declared in a sibling file of a test package). Also: Go's screen of library names is 51 interface method names; concrete standard-library methods go out unmarked, so the name step is off for Go (measured on: 457 binds, 12 right of 15, the 3 wrong all standard-library names, Uint32 alone 50 binds). Nested go.mod files, replace directives and go.work are not read (none on the three trees). Evidence and method: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/batch5b_11262026/ (DESIGN.md with its log; <lang>.md inventories; <lang>_RESULTS.md; maps mine_5b5d against before/; blind judgments judge/judgments_<lang>.jsonl scored by judge/score.py, samples seed 20261125). Found while moving Perl, Ruby, Lua and Go to the shared call resolution (ADR-0064, batch 5b; merged in PR #2426)."  # 3ee2
